# SECRETS - never commit these.
#
# kalshi_private_key.pem is the RSA key that signs your orders: anyone holding
# it can trade on your account. .env carries the key id and the Pyth key.
# A private repo is not protection either, because once a secret is in git
# history it stays there even after you delete the file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p8

# Trading history. Not secret, but these are records rather than code, and
# trades.jsonl grows without limit.
log/
debug/
*.jsonl

# Node
node_modules/
package-lock.json
npm-debug.log*

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Impeccable (reinstall with: npx impeccable skills install)
.agent/
.claude/
.gemini/
